Prerequisites:
==============

1. Install a C compiler
2. Install a version of Tcl compatible with your VMD installation (8.5 or 8.6), including development files (tcl8.6-dev on ubuntu for tcl 8.6, may need to build from source for tcl 8.5)
3. Install zlib (must have zlib.h), note: likely it is already installed
4. Update compile.sh to match the tcl version (8.5 or 8.6)
5. check the includes in the .c file - maybe you need <tcl.h> instead of <tcl/tcl.h> in the includes (e.g. on fedora)
6. run ./compile.sh
7. hope everything works?

